    "jays": {
      "full_name": "Toronto Blue Jays",
      "league": "MLB",
      "record": "19-24",
      "detail": "4th in AL East",
      "lotl": {
        "label": "What's Going On With the Jays",
        "body": "The Blue Jays have spent most of this month looking like a club trying to outrun its own bad habits - then Tuesday's scoreboard finally gave them a little air. <strong>The 5-3 win over the Rays on May 13 snapped the skid and stopped the bleeding.</strong> It was only one game, but after dropping three straight before that, Toronto badly needed a clean finish and a breath of confidence. At 19-24 and 4th in the AL East, 9.5 games back, the Jays are not fooling anybody about the mountain in front of them. This is a team sitting 10th in the playoff picture, one that has spent too much of the spring chasing the division instead of pressing it. The offense has had too many flat nights, and the margin for error is getting thin. Still, a win is a win, and in this business you take the small mercies when they arrive. <strong>Now comes a test in Detroit tonight against the Tigers - another chance to see whether Wednesday was a spark or just a pause.</strong>",
        "updated": "Updated May 15, 2026"
      },
